    "lawCode": "Add §901-a, RPT L",
    "lawSection": "Real Property Tax Law",
    "memo": " \nBILL NUMBER: S2321A\n\nSPONSOR: FAHY\n \nTITLE OF BILL:\n\nAn act to amend the real property tax law, in relation to authorizing\nthe city of Albany to add unpaid housing code violation penalties, costs\nand fines to such city's annual tax levy\n\n \nSUMMARY OF PROVISIONS:\n\nSection 1 adds section 901-a to the real property tax law, authorizing\nthe City of Albany to collect unpaid housing, building and fire code\npenalties by placing them on the City's annual tax levy. Penalties may\nbe added to the levy only if the requirements of section 901a are satis-\nfied, including adjudication by a court of competent jurisdiction, an\noutstanding amount equal to at least five percent of the property's\nassessed tax value, and proper notice by the City, among other require-\nments set forth in the section.\n\nSection 2 sets the effective date\n\n \nJUSTIFICATION:\n\nUnder the Albany Renter's bill of rights, tenants have the right to live\nin housing that is free from code violations and that meets basic stand-\nards of living. Housing stock that is not kept up to code creates neigh-\nborhood blight, which research has shown contributes to health issues\nand public safety risks. Currently, the code enforcement process\ndictates that the City take legal action against landlords who fail to\nfix code violations within 35 days of a complaint. By authorizing the\nCity to include unpaid code violations in the annual tax levy on the\nproperty, this legislation would increase the enforcement capability of\nthe City and would ease the burden on housing courts.\n\n \nLEGISLATIVE HISTORY:\n\nA10738 2019-20\n\nA3128 2021-22\n\nA3957 2023-24\n\n \nEFFECTIVE DATE:\nThis act shall take effect immediately.\n",
